course: dictionary
lesson: 15129
title: Satisfactory: good enough
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how good something is. «Satisfactory» means good enough. It is acceptable and does the job, but it is not excellent. «Your report says satisfactory progress in maths» tells you the teacher is pleased with the work, but thinks there is still room to get better.
explain: The second meaning is about doing what is needed or expected. «The mended bike is satisfactory» means it works and does what a bike should do. To check your meaning, swap it in: "good enough" should still make the sentence make sense.
explain: Be careful: satisfactory is not the same as great. «The results were satisfactory» sounds polite and formal, and it usually means acceptable, not outstanding. The phrase «less than satisfactory» shows that something was not good enough.
fact: Satisfactory means good enough, or acceptable, but not excellent.
fact: Satisfactory can also mean fulfilling what is needed or expected.
fact: «Satisfactory progress» means someone is improving, but not yet brilliantly.
fact: «Less than satisfactory» means not good enough.
fact: The opposite of satisfactory is unsatisfactory, which means not good enough.
exercise: «Your report says satisfactory progress in maths.» What does satisfactory mean here? | Excellent, the best in the class | Late and missing | *Good enough, but there is room to improve | Very loud and noisy
exercise: «The meal was satisfactory: not tasty, but it filled me up.» Which meaning fits? | Delicious and famous | Cold and wet | *Good enough and acceptable | Too big to eat
exercise: Ella says her drawing is satisfactory, not perfect. What does she mean? | It is too small to see | It is the best drawing ever | *It is good enough, but it could be better | It is torn and ruined
test: «The repair was satisfactory, and the tap no longer drips.» What does satisfactory mean? | *Done well enough to do its job | Broken again | Painted gold | Very expensive
test: Which phrase means the work was not good enough? | Happy birthday | Outstanding effort | Very tiny | *Less than satisfactory
exam: The head teacher wrote: «The results were satisfactory.» What does satisfactory mean? | Cancelled | Amazing | *Acceptable, good enough but not excellent | Lost
